{"1-8":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547j","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":2,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":5}],"words":[{"base":"H0589","lemma":"אֲנִי","tr":"a·ni","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":874},{"base":"H5450","lemma":"סִבְלָה","tr":"se·va·lah","gloss":"burden","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H2389","lemma":"חָזָק","tr":"cha·zaq","gloss":"strong","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":56},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":641},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":108},{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":175},{"base":"H1285","lemma":"בְּרִית","tr":"be·rit","gloss":"covenant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":284},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":350},{"base":"H5009","lemma":"נְאָקָה","tr":"ne·a·qah","gloss":"groan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H8478","lemma":"תַּחַת","tr":"ta·chat","gloss":"underneath: under","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":505}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":26,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Then the LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm, with great terror, signs, and wonders.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":68,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Sing to God! Sing praises to His name. Exalt Him who rides on the clouds— His name is the LORD— and rejoice before Him.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":83,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"May they know that You alone, whose name is the LORD, are Most High over all the earth.","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"God said to Moses, “I AM WHO I AM. This is what you are to say to the Israelites: ‘I AM has sent me to you.’”","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"When Abram was ninety-nine years old, the Lordappeared to him and said, “I am God Almighty. Walk before Me and be blameless.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Jacob said to Joseph, “God Almighty appeared to me at Luz in the land of Canaan, and there He blessed me","from":3},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"For you are a people holy to the LORD your God. The LORD your God has chosen you to be a people for His prized possession out of all peoples on the face of the earth.","from":7},{"book":"DEU","chapter":29,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"and so that He may establish you today as His people, and He may be your God as He promised you and as He swore to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"9-13":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":4,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547j","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":3,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":766},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":1142},{"base":"H6547","lemma":"פַּרְעֹה","tr":"par·oh","gloss":"Pharaoh","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":274},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":641},{"base":"H8085","lemma":"שָׁמַע","tr":"sha·ma","gloss":"to hear: hear","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1159},{"base":"H6189","lemma":"עָרֵל","tr":"a·rel","gloss":"uncircumcised","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":35},{"base":"H7186","lemma":"קָשֶׁה","tr":"qa·sheh","gloss":"severe","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"H0349","lemma":"אֵיךְ","tr":"ekh","gloss":"how?","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":82},{"base":"H5656","lemma":"עֲבֹדָה","tr":"a·vo·dah","gloss":"service","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":145},{"base":"H8193","lemma":"שָׂפָה","tr":"sa·phah","gloss":"lips","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":176}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"“Please, Lord,” Moses replied, “I have never been eloquent, neither in the past nor since You have spoken to Your servant, for I am slow of speech and tongue.”","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But in the LORDʼs presence Moses replied, “Since I am unskilled in speech, why would Pharaoh listen to me?”","from":12},{"book":"JER","chapter":1,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"“Ah, Lord GOD,” I said, “I surely do not know how to speak, for I am only a child!”","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Therefore, go! I am sending you to Pharaoh to bring My people the Israelites out of Egypt.”","from":11},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Moses asked God, “Suppose I go to the Israelites and say to them, ‘The God of your fathers has sent me to you,’ and they ask me, ‘What is His name?’ What should I tell them?”","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":29,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Moses and Aaron went and assembled all the elders of the Israelites, and Aaron relayed everything the LORD had said to Moses. And Moses performed the signs before the people, and they believed. And when they heard that the LORD had attended to the Israelites and had seen their affliction, they bowed down and worshiped.","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":5,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"After that, Moses and Aaron went to Pharaoh and said, “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Let My people go, so that they may hold a feast to Me in the wilderness.’”","from":11},{"book":"EXO","chapter":5,"verse":19,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Israelite foremen realized they were in trouble when they were told, “You must not reduce your daily quota of bricks.” When they left Pharaoh, they confronted Moses and Aaron, who stood waiting to meet them. “May the LORD look upon you and judge you,” the foremen said, “for you have made us a stench before Pharaoh and his officials; you have placed in their hand a sword to kill us!”","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]},"14-25":{"people":[{"id":"carmi-h3756g","name":"Carmi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"hanoch-h2585j","name":"Hanoch","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"hezron-h2696g","name":"Hezron","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"pe