b was the father of Nahshon, Nahshon was the father of Salmon,","from":23},{"book":"NUM","chapter":2,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"On the east side, toward the sunrise, the divisions of Judah are to camp under their standard: The leader of the descendants of Judah is Nahshon son of Amminadab,","from":23},{"book":"JOS","chapter":24,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Eleazar son of Aaron also died, and they buried him at Gibeah, which had been given to his son Phinehas in the hill country of Ephraim.","from":25},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Reuben: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Simeon: Jemuel, Jamin, Ohad, Jachin, Zohar, and Shaul the son of a Canaanite woman.","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.","from":16},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Now a man of the house of Levi married a Levite woman,","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":8},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"26-30":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":5,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547j","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":3,"firstVerse":27}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":26}],"words":[{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":641},{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":766},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":1142},{"base":"H6547","lemma":"פַּרְעֹה","tr":"par·oh","gloss":"Pharaoh","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":274},{"base":"H0589","lemma":"אֲנִי","tr":"a·ni","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":874},{"base":"H0175","lemma":"אַהֲרֹן","tr":"a·ha·ron","gloss":"Aaron","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":347},{"base":"H3318","lemma":"יָצָא","tr":"ya·tsa","gloss":"to come out: come","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1067},{"base":"H6189","lemma":"עָרֵל","tr":"a·rel","gloss":"uncircumcised","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":35},{"base":"H0349","lemma":"אֵיךְ","tr":"ekh","gloss":"how?","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":82},{"base":"H8193","lemma":"שָׂפָה","tr":"sa·phah","gloss":"lips","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":176}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":7,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Pharaoh will not listen to you. Then I will lay My hand on Egypt, and by mighty acts of judgment I will bring the divisions of My people the Israelites out of the land of Egypt.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":12,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So you are to keep the Feast of Unleavened Bread, for on this very day I brought your divisions out of the land of Egypt. You must keep this day as a permanent statute for the generations to come.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":12,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And on that very day the LORD brought the Israelites out of the land of Egypt by their divisions.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Go and tell Pharaoh king of Egypt to let the Israelites go out of his land.”","from":29},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But in the LORDʼs presence Moses replied, “If the Israelites will not listen to me, then why would Pharaoh listen to me, since I am unskilled in speech?”","from":30},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron and gave them a charge concerning both the Israelites and Pharaoh king of Egypt, to bring the Israelites out of the land of Egypt.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":7,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"You are to speak all that I command you, and your brother Aaron is to tell Pharaoh to let the Israelites go out of his land.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Thus the heavens and the earth were completed in all their vast array.","from":26}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]}}